<title>ITALY: Italian petroleum consumption up 0.1 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Italian petroleum consumption up 0.1 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian consumption of petroleum</p>
<p>products rose 0.1 percent to 7.3 million tonnes in May, compared</p>
<p>with the same month in 1996, according to data from trade group</p>
<p>Unione Petrolifera.</p>
<p>  Category		     1997 (000 tonnes)  Chg vs 1996</p>
<p>  Total				 7,329		+0.1 pct</p>
<p>  Total petrol			1,503		-0.9 pct</p>
<p>  Total fuel oil		    1,610		-2.6 pct</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>  Total car diesel		  1,292		-3.1 pct</p>
<p>  Total heating oil		   104	     +14.3 pct</p>
<p>Note: Unione Petrolifera said in a statement Italian consumption of petroleum products fell 4.7 percent to 38.08 million tonnes in the first five months of the year compared to the same period in 1996. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
